The 4th QGIS workshop hosted by the **DASV e.V. Digitalization Working Group** will take place online on **July 16, 2026, at 6:00 p.m. sharp**. 

The lecturer will be **[Kai-Christian Bruhn](https://i3mainz.hs-mainz.de/team/kaichristianbruhn/)** from **NFDI4Objects.**

The workshop focuses on **vectorization and mapping in QGIS**. **Requests for additional topics** can be submitted by **July 10** using the following form: **[Link to the form](https://forms.gle/v9E2jkxvNZMo2NmH7)**

Click the following link to join the event on July 16:
**[Zoom link](https://uni-hamburg.zoom.us/j/6486455347?pwd=soCEP79NOZVqJy4P53svE03Ng6rsa7.1&omn=63157524821)**

The event is part of a series of QGIS workshops for archaeologists organized by DASV e.V. in collaboration with NFDI4Objects.

